ime it doesn't look like shigaraki  will reach anywhere close to 100  stabilization rate before the heroes  reached them  so the question is what will fujiko do  now is he going to try to somehow escape  with shigaraki still  inside the tube or is he going to have  to release shigaraki from the tube  prematurely since ujico doesn't seem to  have an escape route in mind  it is possible that he intends to  release shigaraki before he is ready  although it will kill him to do it ujiko  is a lifelong scientist and he considers  shigaraki's procedure to be his  masterpiece  so having to cut it short now and risk  everything  after all the things that he has done to  get to this point must be  killing him but that still leaves us  with the following question  what will happen to shigaraki if he is  forced to emerge from the tube  prematurely is he going to collapse  unable to function properly  is he going to be functioning normally  but he just won't be as strong as he  would have been if he had completed the  procedure  or is he going to be extremely strong  but unable to control himself  so basically an overpowered berserk mode  shigaraki who doesn't have his normal  personality and is just a mindless  machine of destruction  i think that this is the key question  moving forward  what will happen to shigaraki now and  will his release from the tube  be a game changer for the story if  shigaraki emerges stronger than he was  before  and if he is able to function and fight  normally without falling apart or  collapsing or something along those  lines  then the heroes are looking at a deadly  fight against a top-tier  overpowered villain the likes of which  they've never seen before  but as tragic as ujic's failure to  complete his masterpiece is  and i'm sure that every mad scientist  out there can relate to ujico's pain  that was not the tragedy that i was  referring to in the title of this video  the chapter then takes us back to the  undisputed bunny queen  miroko who